DESCRIPTION:Original event page(s):\nhttps://home.dartmouth.edu/events/eve
 nt?event=82224\nhttps://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1CSDcwFdAQplJTqKE6s
 4KSvXqdZRRwqUP/edit?gid=965461601#gid=965461601\n\nDescription:\nIt’s ha
 ppening again! Please join us for the second Summer Tomes\nMoby-Dick\nread
 -athon.\nRead Me Again Ishmael: Another Moby-Dick-athon\nThursday\, August
  20\, 9am-9pm at the Literary Arts Bridge\nFriday\, August 21\, 9am-8pm at
  Still North\nListen to—and help the 26X Summer Tomes cohort read aloud
 —Herman Melville’s very long\, very strange novel of monomania\, monst
 rosity\, manly handholding\, and nautical info dumping. Sign up\nhere\nto 
 claim your favorite chapter! Coffee\, snacks\, and supplementary cetologic
 ally-themed activities will be provided. All are welcome!\n\nSponsor / org
 anizer: English Department\n\nAudience: Public\n\nSource: Dartmouth\n\nWhy
  this was included: Free Food category\; food keyword near service context
 \n\nFood availability is inferred from the source listing\; verify details
  before attending.
