BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Israel's 2026: What to Expect
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260820T163000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260820T180000
DTSTAMP:20260820T102158Z
UID:dartmouth-82260@free-food-dartmouth
SEQUENCE:0
CLASS:PUBLIC
DESCRIPTION:Original event page(s):\nhttps://home.dartmouth.edu/events/eve
 nt?event=82260\n\nDescription:\nIn less than three months\, Israel will go
  to the polls\, in what is expected to be the most polarising elections in
  the country's history\, amidst open ended conflicts in Gaza\, Lebanon and
  with Iran. Public opinion polls suggest the long-term Prime minister Neta
 nyahu is facing electoral defeat. What are the stakes of this election? Wh
 at role do the October 7 attack\, and Israel's three-year war ever since\,
  play in the elections? And what change can they bring?\n\nSponsor / organ
 izer: Jewish Studies Program\n\nAudience: Public\n\nSource: Dartmouth\n\nW
 hy this was included: Free Food category\n\nFood availability is inferred 
 from the source listing\; verify details before attending.
LAST-MODIFIED:20260820T102158Z
LOCATION:Haldeman Hall 41 (Kreindler Conference Hall)
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://home.dartmouth.edu/events/event?event=82260
X-MICROSOFT-CDO-BUSYSTATUS:FREE
END:VEVENT
